From 384dad079e23d81c092fe105d8e8f2f6bf57d99e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xbox360 Blades <xbox360-blades@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 21:20:37 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 38/54] Guide: signed-in menu, Sign Out, profile count, menu
 actions

The Guide shows hud.xex's MainMenuSignedIn when its controller has a
profile signed in (hud 91444010). For a profile without an Xbox Live
account (state 9, 914479E0) that is the gamer card (Mini, with gamerscore,
achievements and picture drawn at run time), the community bar (heading
follows the focus, 91450C18; no counts), Private Chat, Personal Settings,
music and the banner. hud's one-second timer switches menus when the
sign-in state changes.

Menu actions per hud:
- Signed out (91449038 / 91449490): Create New Profile closes the Guide,
  then createprofile. Sign In and X close it, then XamShowSigninUIp (the
  panes are not built yet).
- Signed in (914481F8 / 91448570): the gamer card closes the Guide, then
  gamerprofile. Community and Private Chat go to InfoUpsellLive in the
  Guide (9144851C), and B comes back. X shows the Sign Out box (Strings 39,
  41 / 40, focus No). Yes shows Status.xur ("Signing out", XamUserLogon, at
  least 2 s), then the signed-out menu.

The signed-out menu's labelProfiles ("%d Profiles Found" / "%d Profile
Found", 91449310) now counts the console's profiles.

